From 2fc4c7b65a9d7f9b79c00e9edd3ad1c3e3876ede Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:36:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 222/294] gallium/pvr: per-job end-of-tile program, reference
 free lists, and a geometry-only bisect

The fragment stream's CR_EVENT_PIXEL_PDS_DATA now names a real per-job pixel-event program
instead of a hardcoded offset:

- pvr_csb_pbe_state_words(): PBESTATE_STATE_WORD0/1 (target address, format, MRT, norm, pack
  mode) in the reference's encoding - these are the EOT program's emit inputs, not stream fields.
- pvr_shader_eot_create(): the end-of-tile shader, built as NIR with pco's emitpix intrinsic and
  compiled through the same pco path as the other shaders (pvr_usc.c's pvr_usc_eot equivalent).
- the probe places the USC binary and the PDS pixel-event data segment in their heaps and passes
  the data offset to both draw and liveness fragment streams.

HWRT free lists now match the reference for one device: global 512..65536 pages growing 256 at a
13% threshold, local fixed at the runtime minimum aligned to the free-list size alignment (64 KiB ->
32 pages). The raw 25-page minimum is not a multiple of the page-count granularity the UAPI
requires; CREATE_FREE_LIST then fails EINVAL and every submit fails with it.

Two completion tests make the remaining problem measurable, and they settle where it is NOT:
a geometry-only submission with the draw's stream, and the minimal 40-byte geometry job with an
empty control stream - the latter's firmware stream is dword-identical to the reference's - both are
accepted and never complete. So the stall is in firmware context setup shared by every geometry job,
not in the draw stream, fragment stream, EOT program or free-list configuration.

Verification: probe exits 0 ALL PASS under the noop shim; real-driver run logged in
open-driver-perf/captures/real-runs/probe-real22.txt.
